# release: the flow of depot yardr's releases. A release bead is one version,
# titled "yardr vX.Y.Z": build makes the archives and the GitHub release,
# mckean signs the checksums by hand, verify checks the signature, and
# publish files the yardr.dev sync bead. The script the exec group runs is
# contrib/release/stage; docs/install.md "Making a release" says how a
# release is cut with the yard. A failed verify asks for the signature
# again; anything else failed or questioned waits in decide for a person,
# who advances it to the stage it should retry.
backlog -> build
build -> sign on done | decide on failed | decide on question
sign -> verify on done
verify -> publish on done | sign on failed | decide on question
publish -> published on done | decide on failed | decide on question
decide -> backlog | build | sign | verify | publish
published terminal
